```

`break` leaves, `continue` skips ahead. Same patterns as always: accumulate, count, find the biggest. In Unity, `Update()` runs once per frame: that's a loop the engine runs for you, which is why game code rarely has `while (true)`.

example.code:
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) Console.WriteLine($"7 x {i} = {7 * i}");
        int saved = 0, months = 0;
        while (saved < 1000) { saved += 300; months++; }
        Console.WriteLine($"{months} months");
        foreach (char c in "Habari") Console.Write(c + " ");
    }
}

